  "changes": [
    "ThreadPage and Library now open one frozen export flow; default Markdown output remains the existing default, with an explicit loaded tool-details option implemented by root.",
    "ZIP candidates start unchecked. Local selections use the existing exact-file inspection, received text/bytes stay distinct, and remote references never trigger automatic downloads.",
    "Replacement selection permits deselecting, reselecting and replacing again without dangling replacement metadata. Optional ZIP/detail limits cannot disable the otherwise valid default Markdown variant.",
    "The canonical UTF-8 digest matches real Rust samples. Only the live explicit Save owner can register and start its timely ready preparation; close/picker/hash late results cannot reauthorize another save.",
    "Registered jobs retain safe identity/progress across close and navigation; they join file-save activity and quit protection. Request observation timeout is not worker completion. Closed absent acknowledgement retires only the frontend observation; ordinary unknown still requires backend release.",
    "Registered form and parent captures discard export-owned payload references. The actual IPC may retain its input while pending; this is not a claim of JavaScript memory zeroing or modification of conversation data.",
    "Generated member basenames remain numeric. A fixed ordinary filename suffix whitelist improves PDF/image/Office handoff; unknown/active suffixes fall back to .bin and inline text remains .txt. This is not content or MIME validation."
  ],
